From b58b8da580d6e73fe1dd13be19ef7330d60fe653 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woaphone <woaphone@local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:41:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] rothko: kernel watchdog takeover and memory diagnostics
 (unx3)

unx2 kept running after launchd (heartbeats at 41 s and 51 s) and then reset
silently.  The MT6989 watchdog is armed by the boot chain (MODE=0x7D: enable,
IRQ, dual stage; LENGTH=0xC800, about 25 s per stage) and RothkoWatchdogDxe
only feeds it from a UEFI timer event, which stops after DarwinJump.

- k70u_health_start(): map the WDT at 0x1C00B000 and, while MODE.EN is set,
  write 0x1971 to RESTART once per second from a thread call.  MODE/LENGTH are
  left untouched; a stalled scheduler stops feeding, so a real hang still
  resets.  Every 5 s log pings/MODE/LENGTH/STATUS and a memory snapshot.
- k70u_memory_snapshot(): max_mem, sane_size, free/min/target, wire, active,
  inactive, speculative, compressor pressure, gPhysBase/gPhysSize.
- Snapshots at boot (boot_args phys/memSize), launchd main (initproc_spawned),
  jetsam kills and an empty shared region; log the shared_region map result.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
index 4b44417..09b647d 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#include <kern/k70u_trace.h>
 #include <kern/boot_progress.h>
 /*
  * Copyright (c) 2000-2016 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.
@@ -1342,7 +1343,12 @@ sysctl_initproc_spawned(struct sysctl_oid *oidp, __unused void *arg1, __unused i
 		// Can only ever be set by launchd, and only once at boot
 		return EPERM;
 	}
-	return sysctl_handle_int(oidp, &initproc_spawned, 0, req);
+	int error = sysctl_handle_int(oidp, &initproc_spawned, 0, req);
+	if (req->newptr != 0 && error == 0) {
+		printf("K70U-INIT3: launchd-main=%d\n", initproc_spawned);
+		k70u_memory_snapshot("launchd-main");
+	}
+	return error;
 }
 
 SYSCTL_PROC(_kern, OID_AUTO, initproc_spawned,
